    "offices": {
      "President": "Elected for a four-year term in a modified two-round system: to win in the first round a candidate needs the most votes nationally and over 25% of the vote in at least 24 of the 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory, otherwise a second round, and if needed a third, is held. The president is head of state and of government.",
      "Senate": "The 109 senators are elected for four-year terms by first past the post in single-member districts, three for each of the 36 states and one for the Federal Capital Territory. With the House of Representatives it forms the National Assembly, the federal legislature.",
      "House of Representatives": "The 360 members are elected for four-year terms in single-member constituencies by first past the post. With the Senate it forms the National Assembly, the federal legislature."
    }
